{{Quote|He said the Jedi will always have an ally here on Skako Minor.|Qin Yazal, as [[Language|translated]] by [[Tech]]|<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />}}
'''Skako Minor''', sometimes referred to as simply '''Skako''', was a [[planet]] that was the [[homeworld]] of the [[Poletec]] [[species]]. It was controlled by the [[Techno Union]], whose headquarters was the [[city]] of [[Purkoll]]. Despite the Techno Union's ostensible neutrality, Skako Minor was captured by the [[Galactic Republic]] during the [[Clone Wars]], and its successor, the [[Galactic Empire]], maintained the occupation into the [[Galactic Civil War]].

==Description==
A temperate world, the [[planet]] Skako Minor's misty surface featured canyons, [[mountain]]s, [[cave]]rns, craters,<ref name="Databank" /> and [[Fungus|fungal]] [[forest]]s. It had an atmosphere of [[Hydrogen sulfide|hydrogen sulphide]] that allowed [[Skakoan]]s to live without their [[pressure suit]]s.<ref name="Doctor Aphra 15" /> Other areas of the planet, however, existed in such a state that Skakoans still donned their pressure attire and other species could move about freely.<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" /> Native fauna included the large, flying reptiles<ref name="Poletec" /> known as [[keeradak]]s.<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />

==History==
At some point, industrialist [[Skakoan]]s native to the nearby planet of [[Skako]] traveled to Skako Minor, and eventually the headquarters of the [[Techno Union]] conglomerate were moved to the world after it became predominantly controlled by members of the species.<ref name="Fully Operational">[[Fully Operational (sourcebook)|''Fully Operational'']]</ref> During the [[Separatist Crisis]], the Union's [[Foreman]], [[Wat Tambor]], aligned the Techno Union with the cause of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]], an alliance of disenchanted [[star system]]s led by the charismatic [[Count of Serenno|Count]] [[Dooku]].<ref name="Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}}</ref>

[[File:A_Distant_Echo.png|thumb|left|220px|Echo was held prisoner on Skako Minor.]]
The Union remained officially neutral,<ref name="Fully Operational" /> but supported the Separatists' military efforts during the [[Clone Wars]], including holding the [[Battle of Lola Sayu|captured]] [[Galactic Republic|Republic]] [[Advanced Recon Commando|ARC trooper]] [[Echo]] in a [[Purkoll Tower Base|Techno Union facility]] in the Skako Minor settlement of [[Purkoll]], allowing the Confederacy to exploit a Republic [[Rex's battle strategy algorithm|strategy algorithm]] which Echo knew of against the Republic. In the [[19 BBY|last]] [[Standard year|year]] of the war, a Republic [[Mission to Skako Minor (Clone Wars)|incursion]] would violate the planet's corporate neutrality and free Echo.<ref name="A Distant Echo" /> At the end of the Clone Wars, [[Darth]] Vader killed Wat Tambor. At some point later, Vader embarked on a [[Mission to Skako Minor (Darth Vader)|Mission to Skako Minor]], executing all of Tambor's loyalists<ref name="Vader 28" /> by massacring the [[Ruling Council (Skako Minor)|Ruling Council]]<ref name="Vader 29">[[Darth Vader (2020) 29|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 29]]</ref> and installing a [[Skakoan Council|new regime]] loyal to the [[Galactic Empire]] in its place.<ref name="Vader 28" /> Amongst those Vader killed was [[Wat Tambor II]], the son of the late Techno Union Foreman.<ref name="Vader 29" />

After the war, the Techno Union was known to have been dissolved,<ref name="Fully Operational" /> and Skako Minor came under [[Occupation of Skako Minor|occupation]] by the [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="Doctor Aphra 15" /> the successor state to the Republic.<ref name="Fully Operational" /> Skakoans who protested Imperial rule were exiled from the planet, making life difficult for them as they ran out of the world's special air in their pressure suits.<ref name="Vader 29" /> Despite the fall of the CIS<ref name="ROTS">{{Film|III}}</ref> and the Techno Union,<ref name="Fully Operational" /> Echo&mdash;who, like most members of [[Clone Force 99]], had abandoned the [[Imperial Military]]&mdash;suspected that he would still be trapped within the Techno Union headquarters on Skako Minor if he had never been rescued. He stated as such on the planet [[Daro]], using Clone Force 99's experience rescuing him as a reason to [[Extraction on Daro|extract]] former [[clone commando]] [[Gregor]] from an [[Imperial Base on Daro|Imperial training center]].<ref name="War-Mantle">{{TBB|War-Mantle}}</ref>

[[File:ImperialsOnSkako-2016DoctorAphra15.png|thumb|right|220px|[[Imperial Military|Forces]] of the Galactic Empire on Skako Minor during the [[Son-tuul Pride]]'s [[Mission to Skako Minor (Son-tuul Pride)|mission]] to the planet]]
Between [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]],<ref name="Darth Vader 28 date">The events of [[Darth Vader (2020) 28|''Darth Vader'' (2020) 28]] take place after the [[Escape from Cloud City]] and before the [[Rescue of Han Solo]], which are dated to [[3 ABY]] and [[4 ABY]], respectively, by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''.</ref> a nationalist by the name of [[Jul Tambor]], the grandson of Wat, began efforts to reclaim Skako Minor. He enlisted pirates to [[Blockade of Skako Minor|blockade]] the planet and stockpile technology, but many innocents came to suffer due to his actions.<ref name="Vader 28" /> After pirates attacked Skakoan refugees<ref name="Vader 29" /> the world of<ref name="Vanguard Databank">{{Databank|vanguard-squadron|Vanguard Squadron}}</ref> [[Brentaal IV]], Jul himself claimed to have no links to, at least, those pirates, claiming they were a third party taking advantage of a noble war, which he maintained was being fought for his oppressed people.<ref name="Vader 29" /> In response to the uprising, Vader and the newly-conscripted [[Lieutenant Commander]] [[Sabé]] [[Mission to Skako Minor (Darth Vader and Sabé)|traveled]] to Skako with the aim of finding the nationalist. Only finding pirates,<ref name="Vader 28" /> Vader dispatched Sabé on another [[Mission to Brentaal IV (Sabé)|mission to locate Jul]], who was on Brentaal IV giving Skakoan air to refugees.<ref name="Vader 29" />

==Society and culture==
{{Dialogue|Skywalker|Rex, what do we know about this place?|Rex|On this part of Skako, there's a race of locals, the Poletecs. All we know is they're very primitive.|Tech|Primitive is being kind. My intel says the Poletecs worship flying reptiles.|attr=[[Anakin Skywalker]] receives intel from [[Rex]] and [[Tech]]|src=<ref name="A Distant Echo" />}}
[[File:Poletec-ADE.png|thumb|left|220px|The natives Poletec.]]
Skako Minor was the homeworld of the sentient [[Poletec]] species.<ref name="Poletec" /> It also came to be inhabited by members of the Skakoan species, who could survive without the masks of their pressure suits in some areas of the planet.<ref name="Doctor Aphra 15" /> The Poletec were a primitive species who worshipped large flying reptiles known as keeradaks. They remained neutral during the Clone Wars and lived in small settlements.<ref name="A Distant Echo" /> The rescue mission of Echo would prove to be a turning point for at least one tribe of Poletecs, who fought alongside Republic forces and promised their continued support should the Jedi ever need to return.<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />

==Locations==
{{Quote|Tambor was Skako's most cherished son. For us, his personal workshop is a holy site.|[[Hallio Bas]], on Tambor's personal workspace|<ref name="Doctor Aphra 15" />}}
[[File:SkakoMinor-2016DoctorAphra15.jpg|thumb|right|220px|Skako Minor]]
The Techno Union built their headquarters,<ref name="Databank" /> the [[city]] of Purkoll, on Skako Minor, nearby a Poletec [[Poletec village|village]].<ref name="A Distant Echo" /> It was also the location of a Techno Union [[Wat Tambor's workshop|cache]], which served as the personal workshop of Wat Tambor and was treated as a holy site by the Skakoan people.<ref name="Doctor Aphra 15" />

==Behind the scenes==
{{Quote|The Techno Union owns everything on this planet, including the primitives.|Wat Tambor, in the story reel for "On the Wings of Keeradaks"|<ref name="On the Wings of Keeradaks" />}}
[[File:Skako_Minor_city.jpg|thumb|left|200px|Concept art of the Skako Minor city Purkoll]]
Skako Minor was created for "The Bad Batch" arc of the ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]'' television show, first being mentioned in the episode "[[The Bad Batch (episode)|The Bad Batch]]"<ref name="The Bad Batch">{{TCW|The Bad Batch (episode)}}</ref> and then appearing for the first time in the episode "[[A Distant Echo]]."<ref name="A Distant Echo" /> The episodes were first aired as unfinished production reels in [[2015]].<ref name="SW.com">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-clone-wars-bad-batch-recon|text=''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'' "Bad Batch" Recon|nolive=1}}</ref> During the episodes, several characters refer to Skako Minor as just Skako,<ref name="A Distant Echo" /> but the [[2018]] roleplaying supplement [[Fully Operational (sourcebook)|''Fully Operational'']] established that the two were separate worlds.<ref name="Fully Operational" /> The trivia gallery for "A Distant Echo" also erroneously referred to Skako Minor as "home of the Skakoan people" instead of Skako.<ref name="Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/a-distant-echo-episode-guide|text="A Distant Echo" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

